  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Reverse the logarithm operation",
      "body": "First isolate the logarithm, keeping the outside minus sign separate. A logarithm tells you which exponent of its base gives its argument.",
      "recap": "To undo a logarithm, raise its base to the value of that logarithm.",
      "pitfall": "The outside minus sign changes the logarithm value, not its argument.",
      "pause": "Apply the definition, rearrange for the requested variable and check the original argument is positive.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l06",
          "reminder": "To undo a logarithm, raise its base to the value of that logarithm."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "solution": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math> gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>. By the logarithm definition, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>.</p><p>Therefore <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></math>, which is <strong>D.</strong> Since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>, the expression obeys the original requirement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>.</p>",
